  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-116322",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL pre-authentication cancel request can leak a spinlock",
  "details": "Improper locking in PostgreSQL startup processing allows an unauthenticated network client to trigger a server restart, via arranging for authentication_timeout to arrive while it holds a spinlock during cancel handling.  Within major version 18, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.7 are affected.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18 are unaffected.",
